- `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `addOwner` → requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (`Roles.OWNER_ADMIN`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`).
- Two mutually-exclusive filter chains via `@ConditionalOnProperty(name="petclinic.security.enable")`:
  - `BasicAuthenticationConfig` (value `true`): CSRF disabled, all requests authenticated, HTTP Basic; JDBC authentication against `users`/`roles` tables; `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled=true)` activates the `@PreAuthorize` checks. Defines a `BCryptPasswordEncoder` bean — used to verify **user login passwords**, not owner data. There is no password field on owners and no password encoding in the create flow.
  - `DisableSecurityConfig` (value `false`): all requests permitted (method-level `@PreAuthorize` is not enabled in this profile, so the role check is effectively bypassed).

